yxml
------------------------------------------
Yxml is a small (6 KiB) non-validating yet mostly conforming XML parser written
in C. Its primary goals are small binary size, simplicity and correctness. It
also happens to be pretty fast.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libyxml-devel-0+git20201108-1bl3
  libyxml0-0+git20201108-1bl3
  pkg-config-3.0.10-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cmake-4.4.5-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://dev.yorhel.nl/yxml

Canonical download:
  git://g.blicky.net/yxml.git

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack yxml-0+git20201108-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./yxml-0+git20201108-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/yxml-0+git20201108-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/yxml-0+git20201108-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libyxml0-0+git20201108-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libyxml-devel-0+git20201108-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(yxml)
  /usr/share/doc/Cygwin/yxml.README
  /usr/share/doc/yxml/COPYING

(libyxml0)
  /usr/bin/cygyxml-0.dll

(libyxml-devel)
  /usr/include/yxml.h
  /usr/lib/libyxml.dll.a
  /usr/lib/pkgconfig/yxml.pc

------------------

